# Project Stack

This project uses:

- .NET 9
- C# 13
- Blazor Server
- MudBlazor
- EF Core
- Clean Architecture
- Repository Pattern
- MediatR
- FluentValidation

Always generate production-ready code.

---

# General Principles

Follow:

- SOLID
- DRY
- KISS
- YAGNI
- Clean Code

Avoid hacks.

Avoid duplicated logic.

Prefer readability over clever code.

---

# Language Features

Use modern C# features whenever appropriate:

- Primary Constructors
- Collection Expressions
- File Scoped Namespace
- Global Using
- Target Typed new()
- Pattern Matching
- Required properties
- init setters
- nameof()
- string interpolation
- switch expressions

Do not generate outdated C# syntax.

---

# Naming

Classes:
PascalCase

Methods:
PascalCase

Properties:
PascalCase

Fields:
_privateField

Interfaces:
IRepository

Constants:
PascalCase

Enums:
PascalCase

Enum members:
PascalCase

Private readonly fields start with "_".

Never use abbreviations unless they are domain terms.

---

# Nullable

Nullable Reference Types are enabled.

Never use null when avoidable.

Validate inputs.

Prefer ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull().

---

# Async

Prefer async/await.

Never block using:

.Result

.Wait()

Support CancellationToken whenever possible.

Method names must end with Async.

---

# Dependency Injection

Use constructor injection.

Never use Service Locator.

Never instantiate services manually.

---

# Exceptions

Throw meaningful exceptions.

Never swallow exceptions.

Never catch Exception unless required.

Log unexpected exceptions.

---

# Methods

Methods should:

- Have a single responsibility.
- Stay under 40 lines when possible.
- Avoid deep nesting.
- Prefer early return.

Extract complex logic into private methods.

---

# Classes

Classes should have one responsibility.

Avoid God Objects.

Avoid static helper classes unless truly stateless.

---

# Collections

Prefer:

IReadOnlyList<T>

IEnumerable<T>

Only use List<T> when mutation is required.

---

# LINQ

Prefer readable LINQ.

Avoid multiple enumerations.

Avoid LINQ inside loops.

Avoid complex nested LINQ.

---

# Strings

Use string interpolation.

Avoid string concatenation.

Use StringBuilder for large text generation.

---

# Magic Values

Never use magic numbers.

Never use magic strings.

Use constants.

Use enums.

---

# DTO

Never expose EF entities.

Always return DTOs.

Separate:

Entity

DTO

ViewModel

Request

Response

---

# Validation

Use FluentValidation.

Do not duplicate validation.

Validate as early as possible.

---

# Logging

Use ILogger<T>.

Do not log sensitive information.

Log meaningful context.

---

# Comments

Write self-explanatory code.

Avoid obvious comments.

Comment only:

- business rules
- algorithms
- non-obvious decisions

---

# Performance

Avoid unnecessary allocations.

Avoid boxing.

Prefer Span<T> only when performance critical.

Avoid premature optimization.

---

# Formatting

Use expression-bodied members only when readable.

Keep one blank line between methods.

Use var only when type is obvious.

Otherwise use explicit types.

---

# Output Quality

Generated code must be:

- Production Ready
- Readable
- Maintainable
- Testable
- Extensible

Never generate placeholder implementations.

Never leave TODO comments unless explicitly requested.

Never omit error handling.

Never generate sample/demo code unless requested.